===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|tater}}, from {{der|en|non|tǫturr}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*taturaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*tadǭ|t=tuft, patch}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[shred]] of [[torn]] [[cloth]]; an individual [[item]] of torn and ragged [[clothing]].
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1896|lyricist=William S. Gilbert|composer=Sir Arthur Sullivan|title=Well You're a Pretty Kind of Fellow|passage=You can’t – you shan’t – you don’t – you won’t – you thing of rag and '''tatter''', O!}}

